:- module(constructor_function_collision, [go/0]).
:- chr_constraint go.

% Forbidden: 'foo' is declared as both a data constructor and a
% function in the same module. Both would spell as
% 'constructor_function_collision:foo', so qualifying a reference
% cannot say which is meant — unlike the cross-module case, which is
% legal and diagnosed per bare use as YCHR-20020.
%
% Arity does not separate them either: 'foo/0' the constructor still
% collides with 'foo/1' the function.
%
% The equation below does reference 'foo', and YCHR-20020 still stays
% quiet: its check suppresses itself whenever one module supplies both
% sides, precisely so this error is what the user sees.
:- chr_type t ---> foo ; bar.

:- function foo/1.

foo(X) -> X.

go <=> true.
